      "answer": "The approved live patch window for Verdant Bay is on 2026-03-24 from 02:00 to 04:00 local time, as granted and customer approved.\n\nIf the validation checks fail during the live patch, the rollback procedure is to use the command 'orchestrator rollback --target ruleset=<prior_sha>' which rehydrates the prior rules and replays the cache invalidation hook. After rollback, Verdant Bay is notified, an incident is opened for manual remediation, and any partial replays are reverted.\n\nThe live patch steps include:\n- Taking a pre-patch snapshot of OR-AUDIT-LOGS for the last 30 days.\n- Draining the worker pool in 10% increments and confirming no running approval executions before patching.\n- Deploying the ruleset branch atomically and triggering cache invalidation.\n- Running validation jobs with synthetic and in-flight approvals.\n- If validation passes, release; if any validation fails, execute the automatic rollback as above.\n\nThis rollback procedure and patch plan were discussed and agreed upon with Verdant Bay stakeholders to ensure minimal disruption and compliance evidence export after the patch [art_fff67d92fe41, art_f893faeda15a].",
