      "answer": "The SCIM fields conflicting at Aureum were \"department\" and \"businessUnit,\" which were used inconsistently across teams\u2014Merchant Services used businessUnit=merchant while Payments Ops used department=payments. This inconsistency caused ingestion normalization issues and routing failures in the Rules Engine.\n\nJin proposed a fast fix to avoid waiting on Okta change control by adding a preprocessing rule in Signal Ingest to map \"businessUnit\" to \"department\" (or vice versa) to produce a normalized field for the correlator. This fix is a configuration-only, hot-reloadable change that can be applied quickly without requiring Okta flow changes, thus avoiding the 2\u20134 week delay associated with Okta change control.\n\nThis approach allows immediate normalization and improved routing while a longer-term standardization at the identity source (Okta) is planned. The preprocessing rule can be hot-reloaded with no appliance restarts during sensitive settlement windows, minimizing operational risk. [art_79f625aafa16]",
      "source_ids": [
        "art_79f625aafa16"
      ],
      "retrieved_artifact_ids": [
        "art_545110f843dc",
        "art_79f625aafa16",
        "art_fb836b38496a",
