      "answer": "We do have a recurring Canada approval-bypass pattern across multiple accounts, not just MapleBridge as a one-off. The customers affected by this recurring pattern are City of Verdant Bay, Maple Regional Transit Authority, MapleBay Marketplace, MapleFork Franchise Systems, MaplePath Career Institute, MapleWest Bank, and MapleBridge Insurance.\n\nThe shared failure pattern in plain English is that after migrating from legacy workflow tooling, approval workflows for Canada-specific policies fail because the rules evaluator incorrectly prioritizes global default rules over region-specific (province or country) override rules. This misordering or schema normalization mismatch causes approval tasks to get stuck, auto-denied, bypassed, or routed incorrectly. As a result, manual escalations, approval bypasses, and compliance risks occur. The root cause is a precedence bug in the rules evaluator where global-default policies are prioritized over region-specific overrides, often due to schema normalization issues or delayed synchronization across evaluation clusters [art_cbfb5f92862c, art_6be1b68b59cb, art_39c1434aa40a, art_f4a8c516b934, art_e9c20e0a23e0, art_981952a71434, art_b86a0ca2ce1e, art_ad58f3ce1afd, art_54e35e2cb431, art_e697b3abe158].",
